   "summary": "This 32-page register contains the official index and purport summaries of State Department communications filed under classification 894.24 (document numbers 1558 through 1911) between June 1941 and June 1945. The documents chronicle pre-Pearl Harbor diplomatic negotiations and export restrictions governing petroleum, scrap iron, copper, mercury, rubber, and cotton, including trilateral cooperation among the United States, Great Britain, and the Netherlands East Indies. They also trace Allied intelligence operations to prevent the diversion of strategic Latin American resources to Japan and record wartime inquiries into pre-war trade policy and captured Japanese weaponry.",
